                                                "sense_id": "3bd0255c-032c-3e6c-bdd8-5b5cbdcd5b4d",
                                                "text": "(C. S.) Lewis occasionally expressed a somewhat tongue-in-cheek chauvinism towards the English. Describing an encounter with a fellow Irishman, he wrote: \"Like all Irish people who meet in England, we ended by criticisms on the invincible flippancy and dullness of the Anglo-Saxon race."
